usage: check-recheck-commands.py [-h] (--revision REV | --selftest)
                                 [--paths PATH [PATH ...]] [--exec-log PATH]
                                 [--branch BRANCH] [--forbid LIST]

Read-only recheck-procedure gate (rounds 17-18).

options:
  -h, --help            show this help message and exit
  --revision REV        required: 7-64 hex commit; HEAD/@/refs are rejected
  --selftest            hermetic fixture suite
  --paths PATH [PATH ...]
                        knowledge files or directories; directories expand to
                        their *.md members (default: corpus/knowledge)
  --exec-log PATH       lane-relative log of executed commands (`$ cmd` lines)
                        to check against --forbid at the revision
  --branch BRANCH       branch the revision must be landed on (default:
                        master); validated by tools/_revision.py
  --forbid LIST         comma-separated forbidden binaries
